From: PiSight developers <pisight@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: let disabled recovery own coalesced isoc IN completion

In buffer-DMA isochronous IN mode, XFERCOMPL and EPDISBLD may be
reported together. Completing the request first advances target_frame
and can start the next request. Disabled recovery then flushes its FIFO
and unconditionally retires that next request, even if its target frame
has not elapsed. A Pi Zero trace captured current frame 2361, target
2362 and interrupt bits 0x3 at that erroneous retirement.

Extend the existing NAK completion exclusion to EPDISBLD. Disabled
recovery retires the original request once and leaves the next request
for resynchronization. This conservatively reports ENODATA for the
original transfer even if some or all of it reached the host. Descriptor
DMA and non-isochronous completion paths are unchanged.

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -3128,7 +3128,14 @@
 			 * need to look at completing IN requests here
 			 * if operating slave mode
 			 */
-			if (!hs_ep->isochronous || !(ints & DXEPINT_NAKINTRPT))
+			/*
+			 * Recovery owns the current isochronous request when NAK
+			 * or endpoint-disabled accompanies completion. Completing
+			 * it here can start the next request before recovery flushes
+			 * the FIFO and retires the queue head.
+			 */
+			if (!hs_ep->isochronous ||
+			    !(ints & (DXEPINT_NAKINTRPT | DXEPINT_EPDISBLD)))
 				dwc2_hsotg_complete_in(hsotg, hs_ep);
 
 			if (idx == 0 && !hs_ep->req)
